                <pb facs="0636" n="610" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v03/pg610"/>

                <head>271. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>The President’s Intelligence Checklist, August 23, seen by the President,
                    contains the following item entitled “South Vietnam”: <list>
                        <item>“a. Tight security precautions are still being enforced in Saigon and
                            Hue, but troop presence is less obtrusive.</item>
                        <item>“b. Nhu told a US source yesterday that the generals recommended the
                            imposition of martial law. He denied this amounted to a coup, but warned
                            it could become one if Diem vacillated or compromised on the Buddhist
                            issue.</item>
                        <item>“c. Ambassador Lodge notes that the resignation of Foreign Minister
                            Mau ‘obviously caught the government flatfooted’.” (Kennedy Library,
                            National Security Files, Chester V. Clifton Series)</item>
                    </list></p>
            </div>
